# ── Build outputs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# build/exports/ and build/artifacts/ are gitignored (see CLAUDE.md → Repository
# Layout), EXCEPT manifest.json files inside build/artifacts/, which are the
# build-agent's audit record.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file if a parent directory is excluded, so we ignore
# artifact CONTENTS with `**`, un-ignore the directories themselves so git
# still descends into them, then re-include the manifests.
build/exports/
build/artifacts/**
!build/artifacts/**/
!build/artifacts/**/manifest.json

# ── OS / editor ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.vscode/

# ── Node (Code Apps — React/Vite) ────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/

# ── .NET (plugin assemblies) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
bin/
obj/
*.user

# ── Claude Code local settings ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude/settings.local.json

# NOTE: logs/ and docs/ are intentionally NOT ignored — the system commits its
# routing/build/pipeline logs and generated documents as an audit trail.

# ── Test fixtures ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# src/tests/provisioning/ writes a fully-resolved settings fixture here so the real
# Get-Setting (which fails fast on {{PLACEHOLDER}} tokens) can run, and removes it in
# AfterAll. `acc` is used because this feature documents it as never used — TST and ACC
# are one environment, addressed as `test` (TAD ADR-006). Ignored so a crashed run cannot
# leave a fixture that gets committed and then read as a real settings file.
provisioning/deploymentSettings/acc-settings.json
